--  R7.40: [1350]'s enabled form takes type and fixed parameters and its
--  applications are fully applied and positional.  A fixed integer where
--  a type formal stands is that rule's boundary, which D135 recorded in
--  R2.40; the note says so rather than promising a finished item.
bytes: type (t: type, fixed n: u32) = [n]t
bad: type = bytes(4, 4)
